! The cold read of D2's ground ~ a spirit's handoff, held unedited

''Register: Testimony-Verbatim.'' Nothing below makes this house's own claim. It holds what a tasked spirit reported from reading the tree at `2e8d22d37`, before the wire-socket lane merged (PR #44), kept whole as a ''collision surface''.

''What the house took from it.'' The port's kinds join the vessel and island unions in `island-protocol.ts` beside the camera's kinds, and their readers sit in `lar-camera.ts`; `port:ask` and the invoke gate belong in the island's dispatch (`wiki-behavior.ts`); `port:write` reuses the outbound record path but answers with its own `txId`. The collision map it drew yields to the merged base: wire-socket merged, so D2 edits the shared protocol and composer files on the merged base. Its four pure steps (the recording document and serialisers, the width and local-filter core, the invoke gate, presence expiry) stand as D2's first slices.

''Read it against us, not for us.'' Collide it; do not inherit it.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-handoff`>>

!! The handoff, verbatim

````markdown
<<~ status text=`D2 ground read; handback inline because this read-only workspace supplied no -o path`>>

## 1. What stands for D2

- **Port protocol:** The live island’s existing message unions include `wiki:place-verb` and `wiki:verb-result`, plus camera frame/control/service kinds, but no `port:*` kinds yet. Add the port messages to the vessel↔island unions and their type guards in `island-protocol.ts`; add dedicated readers/factories alongside the camera readers and factories in `lar-camera.ts`. [read: `packages/lararium-mesh/src/island-protocol.ts:750-780,970-1040,1049-1070`; `packages/lararium-mesh/src/lar-camera.ts:301-435`]

- **Live island behavior:** `makeWikiBehavior` already dispatches `wiki:place-verb` to a verb registry and returns `wiki:verb-result`. It supplies a permissive `worker-trust` capability today. D2’s `port:ask` handling and its invoke capability gate belong in the island behavior/dispatch layer, with the gate before `invokeActions`. [read: `packages/lararium-tw5/src/wiki-behavior.ts:103-175`; `bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/dreamdom-roadmap.mem:94-98`]

- **Record waist:** The outbound path already listens to wiki `change`, handles consumed acts, skips foam, then saves or deletes records through `IslandAdaptor`. The adaptor routes writes through the in-wiki `bag-cascade.routeBag`. D2 can reuse that route and record handling; `port:write` needs its own txId/basis request and `port:written` answer, rather than becoming another camera event. [read: `packages/lararium-tw5/src/outbound-bridge.ts:26-46`; `packages/lararium-tw5/src/island-adaptor.ts:365-390`; `bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/dreamdom-roadmap.mem:44-46,96`]

- **Camera contract to reuse:** The camera already gives keyed absolute frames, `cameraId`, mount epochs, revision-aware control events, explicit control answers, and readers that reject malformed messages at the island and vessel doors. D2 should reuse those frame/event mechanics for rendering and invocation references, while carrying records and port asks in their own port message kinds. [read: `packages/lararium-mesh/src/lar-camera.ts:301-435`; `packages/lararium-mesh/src/island-protocol.ts:1007-1069`]

- **Width and tier filter:** The roadmap calls for width as an engine-side field filter and `localFilter` for StoryList, HistoryList, `$:/state`, `$:/temp`, `$:/status`, and `$:/info/browser/*`. Existing worker data verbs provide in-worker read patterns, but they do not implement the port’s width filtering or snapshot/change cursor semantics. These belong in the port’s engine-side module and `port:open`/snapshot/changes handlers. [read: `packages/lararium-tw5/src/worker-data-verbs.ts:1-15`; `bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/dreamdom-roadmap.mem:96`]

- **Recording document and serialisers:** `mountCamera` already accepts a fake document and renders a root template into it. D2’s recording document, blocks/text/label-html serialisers, and missing-camera degradation can live in a new serialiser module beside the camera/engine code; the `blocks` widget-tree pass waits on D5 Annex B. [read: `packages/lararium-tw5/src/tw5-camera.ts:30-71`; `bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/dreamdom-roadmap.mem:96,178-179`]

- **Presence and close:** The roadmap specifies `port:presence` with a 30-second expiry and no persistence, plus `port:close`; width-none presence remains an open ruling whose interim answer uses a separate droppable message. Put those handlers in the port module and the message in the port protocol union. [read: `bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/dreamdom-roadmap.mem:96, the-rulings`; `bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/dreamdom.mem:522-541`]

- **Orphan script:** `meme-worker-script.ts` has no importer in source, tests, scripts, Vite config, or tsconfig; its package export remains. The roadmap calls for retiring it. [read: `bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/tw5-vm-gaps-scout.mem:104`; `bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/dreamdom-harness-scout.mem:157-164`; `bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/dreamdom-roadmap.mem:96`]

## 2. Collisions with wire-socket

The wire-socket range contains commits **“the gate speaks one handshake”** (`c6f52a293`) and **“the socket stands sealed”** (`f7ea58433`), among others. Its diff against the current span changes the browser vessel composer, island protocol, plugin bundle files, web `main.ts`, and a comment in `projection-sink.ts`. [read: `git log origin/feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5..origin/feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5--wire-socket`; `git diff origin/feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5...origin/feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5--wire-socket -- <paths>`]

| D2-touch file | Wire-socket change and collision read |
|---|---|
| `packages/lararium-mesh/src/island-protocol.ts` | Wire-socket removes old auth-verification message types and edits the message unions and guards. **Direct conflict risk:** D2 will add kinds to the same unions/guards. Merge wire-socket first, then add port kinds against its resulting protocol. [read: `git diff … -- packages/lararium-mesh/src/island-protocol.ts`; `git log … -- packages/lararium-mesh/src/island-protocol.ts`] |
| `packages/lararium-browser/src/open-browser-vessel.ts` | Wire-socket restructures boot and relay composition extensively. **Direct conflict risk** if D2 edits this composer for open/close or port routing. Keep D2’s engine/port work elsewhere until wire-socket lands; then add the composer integration. [read: `git diff … -- packages/lararium-browser/src/open-browser-vessel.ts`] |
| `packages/lararium-web/src/main.ts` | Wire-socket changes relay URL, floor card, oracle, and vessel option wiring. **Potential collision** if D2 adds browser startup/open behavior here. Keep port construction in a separate module and wire it after the merge. [read: `git diff … -- packages/lararium-web/src/main.ts`] |
| `packages/lararium-tw5/plugins/*` (four bundle files) | Wire-socket regenerates the bundled memetic-wikitext plugin and attestation. D2 does not need plugin edits for its protocol, serialisers, or engine port. **Avoid this overlap**; if a later D2 change requires plugin content, rebuild after wire-socket lands. [read: `git diff --stat … -- packages/lararium-tw5/plugins`; `git log … -- packages/lararium-tw5/plugins`] |
| `packages/lararium-web/src/projection-sink.ts` | The branch auto-merges with a comment-only wording change. **No substantive conflict shown**, but D2 need not touch this page sink for its engine-side port. [read: `git diff … -- packages/lararium-web/src/projection-sink.ts`] |

**Order:** Let wire-socket merge before D2 edits the shared protocol or browser/web composers. D2 can start its disjoint engine and serialiser modules now. //(inferred from the listed branch diff and D2’s engine-side requirements)//

## 3. D2 pure steps

These can start beside D1 without touching wire-socket files:

- **Recording document and text/label-html serialisers:** new TW5 serialiser module and focused unit tests. Red test: `recording-document-serialisers-render-text-and-label-html`; control: render the same fixture with the existing TW5 camera into its fake document and compare the expected text/link handles. [read: `packages/lararium-tw5/src/tw5-camera.ts:30-71`; `bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/dreamdom-roadmap.mem:96`]
- **Port record/filter core:** new pure engine-side module for width and `localFilter`; no changes to `island-protocol.ts` yet. Red test: `port-skinny-then-load`; control: full width returns the fixture’s complete fields, while skinny omits a named field and an explicit load restores it. [read: `bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/dreamdom-roadmap.mem:96`]
- **Invoke authorization helper:** new capability-gate helper, isolated from the shared protocol and page composers. Red test: `non-admin-invoke-refused`; control: an admin grant invokes the same action and records its call. [read: `bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/dreamdom-roadmap.mem:96`; `packages/lararium-tw5/src/wiki-behavior.ts:145-164`]
- **Presence expiry core:** a pure in-memory expiry tracker; defer message wiring until protocol integration. Red test: `port-presence-expires`; control: a refreshed presence remains visible before 30 seconds and expires after the deadline using a controlled clock. [read: `bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/dreamdom-roadmap.mem:96`]

//(These are proposed test names and controls, not existing tests.)//

I could not write a `-o` file: no output path appeared in the request, and this workspace grants read-only filesystem access.
````

